  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>One thing to know upfront</h2>
      <p>There's no lake or river you can swim in right next to Cavalaire-sur-Mer — the nearest watercourses don't allow swimming. Lake Saint-Cassien is the most realistic freshwater option in the area, but it's about an hour's drive away, and one rule applies everywhere: swimming animals in the lake is banned, according to the Pays de Fayence tourist office. An EDF reservoir, the lake is used for electricity production and drinking-water supply.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A large reservoir lake, 7 km by 3.5 km, between Montauroux, Callian, Tanneron and Les Adrets-de-l'Estérel, in the Var right next to the Alpes-Maritimes. According to the Pays de Fayence tourist office, dogs on a leash are allowed on the lake's beaches, including the supervised Tanneron beach (below the Maison du Lac), but <strong>swimming is banned for animals</strong>. On the Fondurane biotope, a leash is compulsory.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The area most often mentioned for a dog-friendly walk outside the supervised sectors is Plage de l'Américain, chemin du Gabinet in Montauroux (Plage du Pré Claou, just before the bridge, is another option). Pine woods line some areas, offering welcome shade in summer. Parking is free in the designated areas around the lake. Remember to bring water for your dog separately — even though the lake is visible and within sight, there's no question of letting your companion paddle in it.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: given the distance from Cavalaire, I treat this more as a day trip than a habit — but the change of scenery (pine woods, freshwater nearby) is nice once in a while, even without a swim for the dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Pays de Fayence, just above the lake, has other waterways where dog swimming is possible, such as the <a href="/en/fiche-gorges-blavet">Gorges du Blavet</a> or the <a href="/en/fiche-pont-mons-siagnole">Pont de Mons on the Siagnole</a>. Towards Tanneron, the <a href="/en/fiche-gorges-siagne">Gorges de la Siagne</a> round out a trip in this area between the Var and the Alpes-Maritimes.</p>
    </div>

